# Case: Production peer to real guest clipboard
# Mode: native
# Environment: disposable-guest
# Purpose: Verify incoming production synchronization reaches the native clipboard without sender echo.
# Steps:
#   Enable sync through settings; pair an owned production peer with fingerprint approvals; submit synthetic peer text and read the real guest clipboard and remote history.
# Expected:
#   Native clipboard and remote history contain the exact received text; sender history gains only its submitted item; both owned services exit at cleanup.
# Forbidden:
#   Claims of two graphical endpoints, shared clipboard propagation, skipped approvals or directory clipboard substitution.

system-board-write 'UNIC-D receive startup baseline'
start
ui-click listItem 设置…
ui-wait listItem 同步
ui-click listItem 同步
ui-enabled switch 启用同步
ui-click switch 启用同步
config-equals sync.enabled true
connect-policy-peer
system-peer-text 'UNIC-D received native 中文'
screenshot real-clipboard-received
